      "math_academy_id": "e-10022",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{8z^3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first write $8z^3$ as the product $4z^2 \\cdot 2z$ which contains a perfect square $(4z^2){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{8z^3}&=\\[3pt]\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we can separate the product into two separate radicals:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\sqrt{4z^2 \\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2\\cdot 2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the radical containing the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n        \\sqrt{(2z)^2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n        |2|\\cdot|z|\\cdot \\sqrt{2z}&=\\[3pt]\n\t2|z|\\sqrt{2z}&\n\t}\n$$",
